diff --git a/docs/push-notifications.md b/docs/push-notifications.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..8026578
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/push-notifications.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+## Web push notifications
+
+Set `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` to the matching, URL-safe Base64
+VAPID key pair supplied by your operator. Provide both variables to the web app
+and background-job workers, and keep the same pair across deploys. Only the
+public key is exposed to browsers; keep the private key in your secret store.
+Without both keys, push delivery and the push notification settings are disabled.
+
+For a new installation, a pair can be generated once with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"; puts "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+For Kamal, add both names to `env.secret` and supply their values through
+`.kamal/secrets` or your password manager. For Docker, pass them as environment
+variables. Do not commit the values to source control.
+
+Run database migrations and ensure background jobs are running (`bin/jobs`, or
+`SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA=true`). Workers need outbound HTTPS access to browser push
+services. The app must be served over HTTPS (localhost is allowed for development).
+
+Users turn push on in **Notification Settings → Push notifications** on each
+device. On iOS, install Fizzy on the Home Screen and enable notifications from
+the installed app. Blocked or unsupported browsers show installation and
+permission help in settings.
+
+Pushes use the same title and body as the tray, and clicking opens the relevant
+card, including the comment anchor when applicable. Turning push off removes
+only the current device for the current account; email preferences, other devices,
+and other accounts are unchanged. Expired subscriptions are removed automatically.
+Subscriptions are origin- and key-specific and are not included in account exports.
